mapping "b176.1" source="b176" target="SNOMED_CT:304645009" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b176 SNOMED CT 304645009 = ICF b176 Mental function of sequencing complex movements: the
        higher-level mental (frontal/executive) function of planning and ordering complex, sequential,
        coordinated voluntary movements (a cognitive-motor sequencing function, NOT raw motor
        coordination itself — clinically the function impaired in ideomotor/ideational dyspraxia).
        Target SNOMED CT 4128100 (sctid 304645009) =, active RF2 production. This is the only SNOMED CT
        observable that captures sequencing-as-a-mental-ability (rather than 106164003 is the
        motor-execution side, not the cognitive-sequencing side). Broader rather than exact: 304645009
        is a generic logical-sequencing ability (any domain) where ICF b176 is specifically movement
        sequencing; the target fully subsumes the source's domain but is not co-extensive with it. Low
        tier : defensible but real doubt — is broader and more cognitive than the motor-sequencing
        specificity of b176, and there is no independent Athena crosswalk re-verified. (Alternate
        106164003 was rejected: it denotes motor execution, not the mental sequencing ICF b176
        specifies.)
        """
}
mapping "b180.1" source="b180" target="SNOMED_CT:285231000" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b180 SNOMED CT 285231000 = ICF b180 Experience of self and time functions: the chapter-level
        grouping of b1800 Experience of self, b1801 Body image, b1802 Experience of time (a multi-block
        chapter anchor). No single SNOMED CT observable spans both self-experience AND time-experience; the
        only defensible standard target is the broader mental-function observable. Target SNOMED CT 4111207
        (sctid 285231000) =, active, which fully subsumes all b180 sub-functions as mental functions.
        Broader: the target is a true ancestor (every self/time experience function is a mental
        function) but many levels above, and also covers unrelated mental functions, so it is a deep
        broader climb. Low tier : clinically defensible ancestor but loose (multi-hop climb, no
        independent crosswalk); the specific children b1800/b1801/b1802 each get their own tighter
        proposals below. Mapping the chapter block to the general mental-function observable preserves
        the ancestor lead without over-claiming equivalence.
        """
}
mapping "b1800.1" source="b1800" target="SNOMED_CT:225510008" relationship=source_is_narrower_than_target {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1800 SNOMED CT 225510008 = ICF b1800 Experience of self: the mental function of being aware
        of one's own identity and of one's separate distinctness from others and from the environment
        (self-awareness / self-identity as a function). Target SNOMED CT 4021351 (sctid 225510008) =,
        active. This is the closest SNOMED CT observable to a self-experience concept; it captures the
        self-as-experienced (one's image/representation of self), which overlaps heavily with ICF's
        experience-of-self function. Broader rather than exact: is narrower than ICF b1800 in one axis
        (self-image is a component of the broader experience-of-self, which also includes
        self-identity-as-distinct-from-others), but SNOMED CT's only adjacent findings (704447001,
        24340004) are deficit findings, not functions. Because the chosen target is the most-correct
        single observable and is one axis of a multi-axis source, but is the best available standard
        concept, this is assessed as broader (self-image subsumes the representational core of
        experience-of-self) at moderate tier : best-available defensible target, term-verified in the
        mirror, but the SNOMED CT self-image concept does not fully denote the ICF experience-of-self
        function and there is no independent crosswalk. (Note direction: target is broader — it is a
        single observable representing the closest standard lead.)
        """
}
mapping "b1801.1" source="b1801" target="SNOMED_CT:405045001" relationship=equivalent {
    confidence 0.87 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1801 SNOMED CT 405045001 (Kroppsbild) = ICF b1801 Body image: the mental function
        representing one's physical self — the experience and representation of one's own body. Target
        SNOMED CT 4234505 (sctid 405045001) =, active RF2 production, exact literal term match. Exact 1:1
        equivalence: identical clinical concept (body image as an experienced representation of one's
        body), confirmed by literal FSN term match in the Swedish SNOMED CT mirror. (277813003 is a
        finding, not the function/observable; 405045001 is the function-level observable that matches
        ICF b1801.) High tier : exact term match and clear concept equivalence, but no independent
        Athena crosswalk re-verified, so snapped just below. mapping_type=exact_match.
        """
}
mapping "b1802.1" source="b1802" target="SNOMED_CT:247723007" relationship=related_to {
    confidence 0.03 scheme="vocabmod-se-confidence@1"
    comment "en" """
        Source b1802 SNOMED CT 247723007 = ICF b1802 Experience of time: the mental function of the
        subjective experience of time (duration, rate, passage of time) — a function/ability. Target
        SNOMED CT 4085034 (sctid 247723007) =, active, Swedish synonym. This is the only SNOMED CT concept
        covering subjective time-experience, and it is a deficit FINDING (changed/abnormal perception of
        time), not a normal function/observable. The source is a FUNCTION (b1802, including normal time
        experience); the target is the abnormal finding associated with its impairment. This is a
        clinical association, not identity/ancestor/descendant/component — the target is the disorder
        counterpart of the source function. Per the related-vs-no_match boundary rule, there IS a real
        defensible clinical association worth a reviewer's time (the only time-experience concept in
        SNOMED CT), so this is related at low tier, not no_match. (No function-level time-perception
        observable exists in SNOMED CT; a no_match would discard the only lead.)
        """
}
